<plain>
<text x="-68.58" y="25.4" size="5.08" layer="94">RICE ECLIPSE
</text>
<text x="-83.82" y="15.24" size="3.81" layer="94">Avio R&amp;D-Transponder</text>
<text x="-20.32" y="7.62" size="3.81" layer="94">1A
</text>
<text x="226.06" y="25.4" size="5.08" layer="94">RICE ECLIPSE
</text>
<text x="210.82" y="15.24" size="3.81" layer="94">Avio R&amp;D-Transponder</text>
<text x="274.32" y="7.62" size="3.81" layer="94">1A
</text>
<text x="-68.58" y="-205.74" size="5.08" layer="94">RICE ECLIPSE
</text>
<text x="-83.82" y="-215.9" size="3.81" layer="94">Avio R&amp;D-Transponder</text>
<text x="-20.32" y="-223.52" size="3.81" layer="94">1A
</text>
<text x="226.06" y="-205.74" size="5.08" layer="94">RICE ECLIPSE
</text>
<text x="210.82" y="-215.9" size="3.81" layer="94">Avio R&amp;D-Transponder</text>
<text x="274.32" y="-223.52" size="3.81" layer="94">1A
</text>
<text x="-271.78" y="175.26" size="3.81" layer="97">JP1, JP3, JP4 are header pins used for debugging</text>
<text x="-273.05" y="193.04" size="6.4516" layer="97">CC1200
</text>
<text x="-271.78" y="180.34" size="3.81" layer="97">VDD CC1200 is just a filtered 3.3V line, connected via power layer
</text>
<text x="20.32" y="99.06" size="6.4516" layer="97">NEO-M9N
</text>
<text x="20.32" y="210.82" size="6.4516" layer="97">1.5 GHz Coupler and Active Patch Antenna</text>
<wire x1="15.24" y1="118.11" x2="278.13" y2="118.11" width="0.1524" layer="97"/>
<text x="172.72" y="180.34" size="3.81" layer="97">The ANN-MB5 was chosen as the active patch
antenna because it is compatible with the 
NEO-M9N, alternatives can be used assuming
they're also compatible</text>
<text x="172.72" y="161.29" size="3.81" layer="97">J5 and J2 are the SMA ports, J5 is the 
patch antenna</text>
<text x="172.72" y="142.24" size="3.81" layer="97">If using a different coupler remember to
account for coupling factor</text>
<text x="19.05" y="-33.02" size="6.4516" layer="97">JST 12-Pin Connector 
and Header Pins</text>
<wire x1="15.24" y1="-163.83" x2="275.59" y2="-163.83" width="0.1524" layer="97"/>
<wire x1="15.24" y1="-101.6" x2="275.59" y2="-101.6" width="0.1524" layer="97"/>
<wire x1="179.07" y1="-96.52" x2="179.07" y2="-16.51" width="0.1524" layer="97"/>
<text x="182.88" y="-22.86" size="6.4516" layer="97">Mounting Holes</text>
<text x="16.51" y="-110.49" size="6.4516" layer="97">RF Filter and Coupler</text>
<text x="16.51" y="-171.45" size="6.4516" layer="97">CC1200 Power Filter</text>
<text x="182.88" y="-110.49" size="3.81" layer="97">J3 is an SMA port</text>
<text x="182.88" y="-125.73" size="3.81" layer="97">TXPA, TRX, LNA P, and LNA N are all 
RF traces</text>
<text x="182.88" y="-134.62" size="3.81" layer="97">U1 is the RF Filter</text>
<text x="92.71" y="-181.61" size="3.81" layer="97">VDD CC1200 stays at 3.3V, but is filtered for noise</text>
<text x="69.85" y="-55.88" size="3.81" layer="97">JP5 is a 2x1 header pin that serves as 
another test point to evaluate the power and 
ground, belongs near the CC1200</text>
<text x="69.85" y="-83.82" size="3.81" layer="97">JP6 is the JST 12-pin Connector, it connects 
to a microcontroller on a separate board, a 
microcontroller is necessary for operation</text>
<text x="-275.59" y="-172.72" size="3.81" layer="97">LNA_EN_LP and PA_EN_LP are both connections to GPIO pins on the microcontroller</text>
<text x="-275.59" y="-182.88" size="3.81" layer="97">VDD CC1190 is also 3.3V</text>
<text x="-275.59" y="-193.04" size="3.81" layer="97">J4 and J1 are SMA ports, J4 is for the antenna</text>
<text x="-275.59" y="-208.28" size="3.81" layer="97">HY2 is a 915 MHz coupler, if using different make sure to check 
coupling factor</text>
<text x="-275.59" y="-217.17" size="3.81" layer="97">C37 doesn't need to placed</text>
<text x="-275.59" y="-25.4" size="6.4516" layer="97">CC1190 and Whip Antenna</text>
</plain>
